+Uploads are retryable too: `client.Files.Upload` buffers the file into a
+replayable multipart body, so `POST /files` retries on 429 like every other
+call, even when the content comes from an `*os.File`:
+
+```go
+f, _ := os.Open("contract.pdf")
+defer f.Close()
+
+file, err := client.Files.Upload(context.Background(), "contract.pdf", f)
+```
+
+`Files.Add` and `Files.Update` buffer their bodies the same way; a request
+whose body cannot be replayed (for example, a streamed reader passed through
+`Raw().Do`) is sent once and never retried.
+
